abstract: >-
  An open-source framework that derives SUMO network geometry, vehicle demand,
  and signal phase data entirely from fixed-infrastructure LiDAR and roadside
  unit deployments, requiring no manual network editing and no OpenStreetMap
  import. Release 0.1.0 provides the extraction and network generation stages:
  detections are read from rosbag2 archives, road axes are fitted to the
  observed vehicle scatter by singular value decomposition, and the junction
  centre is estimated as the least-squares intersection of those axes. Geometry
  was derived independently from six 30-minute recordings spanning peak,
  off-peak, and overnight conditions at a four-approach signalized
  intersection, reproducing a pooled junction centre of (3.51, 2.91) m from
  over 548,000 vehicle detections. Trajectory extraction, SUMO replay, and the
  performance metrics suite are being ported from the research implementation
  and will follow in subsequent releases.
